            <title>[LU-21279] client oops in lov_lsme_pack_v1v3() for a layout component with an unknown pattern</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21279</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;A client that reads the layout of a file with a component whose pattern it does not recognize oopses in lov_lsme_pack_v1v3(), e.g. "lfs getstripe" of such a file:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;lov: unrecognized striping pattern: rc = 0
lov_dump_lmm_common()) objid 0x5:1026, magic 0x0bd10bd0, pattern 0x5
lov_init_composite()) lustre-clilov-...: unknown layout entry 1 pattern 0x5 could be an unrecognizable component set by other clients, skip to initialize the next component.
BUG: kernel NULL pointer dereference, address: 0000000000000000
RIP: 0010:lov_lsme_pack_v1v3+0x90/0x120 [lov]
 lov_lsm_pack+0x1d8/0x450 [lov]
 lov_object_layout_get+0x157/0x2f0 [lov]
 ll_getxattr_lov+0x1de/0x410 [lustre]
 ll_xattr_get+0x129/0x1a0 [lustre]
 __vfs_getxattr+0x7e/0xb0
 do_getxattr+0x129/0x180
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16837" title="interop: client skip unknown component mirror" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-16837"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-16837&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/51060" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/51060&lt;/a&gt;, "llite: handle unknown layout component") made lsme_unpack() allocate no lsme_oinfo[] for a component whose pattern is not lov_pattern_available(), but it keeps lsme_stripe_count and the INIT flag.  lsme_free() and dump_lsm() skip the objects of such a component (and &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/52826" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/52826&lt;/a&gt; fixed lov_delete_composite()), but lov_lsme_pack_v1v3() still packs lsme_stripe_count objects from lsme_oinfo[].&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Seen on master v2_17_62 with an EC parity component that LFSCK rebuilt with the RAID0|PARITY pattern, which master no longer accepts since LOV_PATTERN_PARITY stands alone (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20690" title="FLR-EC: handle '--ec k+p' components with p &amp;gt; k" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20690"&gt;LU-20690&lt;/a&gt;).  The same applies to any pattern a newer server or client sets that this client does not know.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Parsing the objects of such a component regardless of its pattern would let getxattr return them, so that copying the layout (e.g. lfs migrate, mirror split) does not drop them.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
